    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d958">

                <pb facs="0892" n="788" sameAs="frus:frus1913/pg788"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 812.00/7013.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The American Ambassador to the Secretary of State.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegrams—Paraphrases.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">American Embassy</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Mexico City</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1913-04-04">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">April 4, 1913</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>163. The Government is in control from the State of Durango south, with the
                    exception of unimportant bands in Sinaloa and Zapata’s forces in Morelos, the
                    latter greatly reduced.</p>
                <p>As to Coahuila, Durango, and Nuevo Leon, I believe conditions will steadily
                    improve.</p>
                <p>The Government expects to suppress at an early date the Sonora rebellion.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Henry Lane Wilson</hi>.</signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
